index 0000000..2c9d1ad
--- /dev/null
+++ b/rtabmap_odom/test/CALIBRATION_CACHE.md
@@ -0,0 +1,39 @@
+# Experimental immutable CameraInfo input
+
+This isolated overlay declares `cache_camera_info` (default false). For existing
+launch files that do not forward it, `RTABMAP_CACHE_CAMERA_INFO=1` selects the
+default; an explicit ROS parameter override wins. No production launch changes
+are required. Timing tracing is separately enabled by `RTABMAP_TIMING_AUDIT=1`.
+
+Only raw, aligned, equal-resolution RGB/depth input is supported. Image/depth
+use the existing approximate/exact sync setting, queue size and max interval.
+CameraInfo is observed independently. The first valid calibration is copied;
+subsequent identity includes every field except header stamp. No frames older
+than the first calibration are accepted. Calibration changes/invalid values,
+image frame/dimension mismatches, or non-increasing accepted image/depth times
+latch the input closed until node restart. The cached copy is stamped for each
+image; the source message is never mutated.
+
+The camera must keep calibration fixed throughout a session. There is no cache
+expiry: disconnecting CameraInfo does not stop established image processing.
+A delayed change cannot be detected retroactively, and an already queued/in-flight
+odometry update may finish after a fault is observed. This is not a certified
+interlock and must not be connected to PX4 on the strength of replay results.
+
+Odometry reset retains the immutable identity, fault, timestamp floor and bounded
+pair queues. Synchronizers are not reconstructed from the reset service thread.
+Restart the node for a new time epoch or calibration. Paused input still advances
+the cache's monotonic timestamp check, without invoking the odometry core.
